==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Its a pretty straightforward stage in chapter 1. It is recommended that you use only 3 meatshields, [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] (if you have her) and one other good AoE unit, preferably [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] or [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]]. Pair those with [[Sexy Legs Cat|Sexy Legs]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] and any hard hitting or anti-Dark uber/units available to you and you'll be good to go.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Chapter 2 increases the strength of both types of Kang Roos and you will see extra Shadow Boxer Ks spawn with the boss wave. Ring Girl Cat is almost a must-have here but since she's Super Rare people may not have her yet. The level can still be won without anti-Dark units if you use a Rich Cat and protect your heavy hitters behind more than 3 meatshields.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Chapter 3 is very tough, especially without good anti-Dark units. Excellent timing and precise unit summoning are key to making it out of this nightmare stage alive.

This time around you will no longer see the regular Snaches as peons, they are replaced with 250% Gabriels to bring the total to 4 different kinds of Doges appearing as the only peons in the stage.

The Doges can be overwhelming and you can't really stack Bahamuts because you don't have the time. You need a large force to hold off the doges but once you build up a big force they stop entirely and your army heads to the base.

Even with a Rich Cat you have to summon units to stop the doge wave so you may be able to save up 12k by the time you run out of Doges to farm. You should however, have a substantial force of Damage dealers and enough cash to purchase Bahamut + an Uber before you advance to the base.

When you hit the base, multiple Kang Roos and Shadow Boxer Ks burst out of the base. You can feel like you're doing very well against the first couple Shadow Boxers but soon they'll start pushing you back and you won't stand a chance if they get through your meatshields. Cat CPU is a great help here for perfect Meatshielding, as long as you have all your expensive Units summoned so it doesn't fail.

